.venv/
__pycache__/
.vscode/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
bin/
# soundfonts/* (not soundfonts/) - a bare directory-name rule makes git
# treat the whole directory as opaquely ignored and never look inside it
# even for a later negation, so the exception below would silently not
# apply; soundfonts/* ignores its CONTENTS instead, which negation can
# still see through.
soundfonts/*
# Exception: recall_score_sounds.sf2 is a small, project-authored soundfont
# built by tools/wav_to_sf2.py (click metronome/position announcer sounds,
# Ref 14/28) - unlike FluidR3_GM.sf2 above (~148 MB, third-party,
# load-bearing gitignore per CLAUDE.md's "Local binaries" section), this one
# is only a few hundred KB and belongs in git like any other project asset.
# Regenerate it with the tool rather than editing it directly if the source
# WAVs (tools/*.wav, tools/config.ini) change. No .sf2.json sidecar
# anymore - the tool used to also write one (per-sample duration, for
# SynthEngine to hold a one-shot note on for at least that long), but that
# turned out to be unnecessary once SynthEngine stopped scheduling an early
# note-off at all - see audio/synth_engine.py's play_click() comment.
!soundfonts/recall_score_sounds.sf2
# tools/wav_to_sf2.py's own config (tools/config.ini) writes its .sf2
# output into tools/ itself (output paths are relative to the config
# file's own location) - a disposable build byproduct duplicating the
# real, committed copy above, not source itself.
tools/*.sf2
output.txt
Product Definition Document.html
*.png

# Windows installer build output (packaging/build_installer.ps1, M2) -
# regenerated from source every run, not source itself.
/build/
/dist/
/dist_installer/
packaging/version_info.txt
